WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:02.530
- [Narrator] Coverage of the
ongoing conflict in Israel

00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:05.240
has featured recurring images like this.

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:09.023
Missiles streaming across the
sky and exploding mid-air.

00:00:10.069 --> 00:00:11.200
(explosion popping)

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.580
These are missiles from Israel's

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:14.910
Iron Dome missile defense system,

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:17.400
a land-based system that
intercepts and destroys

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.243
short-range rockets and mortars.

00:00:19.243 --> 00:00:21.830
(missile whooshing)

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:24.190
It has become a bedrock
of the country's defense

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.660
since its introduction in 2011,

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:28.650
and in the current round of hostilities,

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:30.380
Israel's military said the system

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:32.390
has intercepted more than 200

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:34.040
of the more than 1,000 rockets

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:36.393
fired towards Israel as of May 12th.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.010
Here's how the complex detection

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:40.963
and interception system works.

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:44.670
The system is powered by
missile defense batteries,

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:47.113
each containing three main components.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.590
These batteries can defend
across short-range rocket

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:53.913
and mortar attacks within
almost 45 miles of the battery.

00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:55.800
They are also mobile,

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:58.910
so they can be moved to
where they are needed.

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:01.370
First, a radar unit
detects an incoming rocket

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:04.100
and relays information about
its speed and trajectory

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:06.010
to the battery's control center.

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:07.950
The control center's computers calculate

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:11.280
if the rocket is going
to hit populated areas.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.050
If it is, a missile is
fired from the launcher.

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:17.400
Each launcher contains
20 interceptor missiles.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:19.460
Each receives constant guidance updates

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:22.290
from the control center
and its internal radar.

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:24.080
The missile destroys the incoming rocket

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:25.510
by exploding near it.

00:01:25.510 --> 00:01:28.650
The goal is to do this far
away from populated areas,

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:30.920
minimizing damage on the ground.

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:34.140
The defense system has
intercepted over 2,400 rockets

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:37.550
bound for civilian areas
since its launch in 2011

00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:40.320
according to an Israeli
military spokesperson.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:42.280
During a conflict in 2012,

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:44.980
the Iron Dome knocked down 421 rockets

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:47.450
launched from Gaza and
bound for Israeli cities

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:49.740
before a November ceasefire,

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:52.050
and during the 2014 war in Gaza,

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:55.810
it intercepted 700 rockets fired
by Islamist movement Hamas,

00:01:55.810 --> 00:01:58.400
a 90% success rate that
effectively blunted

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:00.800
the Palestinian group's aerial threat.

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:02.140
The United States has provided

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:05.250
hundreds of millions of dollars
and funding for the system

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:07.180
and has also bought and is testing

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:09.660
two Iron Dome batteries of its own,

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:11.810
and Israel has expanded the defense system

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:13.800
by installing missile batteries on ships,

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:16.380
and the system is in the
midst of being upgraded

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:19.060
to combat the threat
posed by unmanned drones.

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:21.130
As the current conflict continues,

00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:23.163
so will the use of the Iron Dome.

